## M. Test / validation SQL

### Duplicate detection

```sql
SELECT 'students_dup' AS issue, student_number, email, university_id, count(*)
FROM students
GROUP BY student_number, email, university_id
HAVING count(*) > 1;

SELECT 'lecturers_dup' AS issue, staff_number, email, university_id, count(*)
FROM lecturers
GROUP BY staff_number, email, university_id
HAVING count(*) > 1;
```

### Foreign-key integrity

```sql
SELECT a.table_name, a.column_name, a.constraint_name
FROM information_schema.constraint_column_usage a
LEFT JOIN information_schema.table_constraints b ON b.constraint_name = a.constraint_name
WHERE b.constraint_type = 'FOREIGN KEY';
```

### Identity validation

```sql
SELECT *
FROM students s
LEFT JOIN users_student us ON us.university_id = s.university_id AND us.student_id = s.student_number
WHERE us.id IS NULL;
```

### Attendance uniqueness

```sql
SELECT session_id, student_id, count(*)
FROM attendance
GROUP BY session_id, student_id
HAVING count(*) > 1;
```

### Biometric validation

```sql
SELECT sb.id, sb.student_id, s.id
FROM student_biometrics sb
LEFT JOIN students s ON s.id = sb.student_id
WHERE s.id IS NULL;
```

